Chapter: SimplifyCheck

 The shapes:

  - sc-fold: a literal let feeding integer arithmetic  -> 5
             (propagate 2, fold 2 + 3)
  - sc-cmp:  a literal let feeding a comparison in an   -> 1
             if condition (propagate 4, fold 4 < 10 to
             True, take the then-arm)
  - sc-neg:  negate of a propagated literal             -> -4
             (propagate 5, fold -5, fold -5 + 1)
  - sc-bool: a boolean or of two literals deciding an   -> 7
             if (fold True or False to True, take the
             then-arm)
  - sc-text: a folded text builtin                       -> 5
             (fold text-length "hello")
  - sc-dead: a pure-valued let never used in the body    -> 42
             (drop the dead binding u = n + 1, fold 6 * 7)
  - sc-copy: copy propagation through two name-bindings   -> 100
             (a = n, b = a both propagate; n + 100)
  - sc-once: a pure value used exactly once, inlined      -> 9
             (s = n * n folds into its single use, + 9)
  - sc-cap:  an ADVERSARIAL capture case that must NOT     -> 2
             inline: x = n cannot be propagated into
             `let n = x + 1 in n * 2` because the inner
             let binds n, the value's own free name. The
             simplifier must SKIP it. If it wrongly inlines,
             the answer changes - and the fixed point cannot
             see that, so this diff is the real guard.
  - sc-lamcap: the same hazard through a LAMBDA binder      -> 10
             rather than a let - x = n cannot inline into
             `(\n -> x + n) 10`; exercises the lambda path
             of the capture check.

Section: Shapes

  sc-fold : Integer -> Integer
  sc-fold (n) = let x = 2 in x + 3

  sc-cmp : Integer -> Integer
  sc-cmp (n) = let m = 4 in if m < 10 then 1 else 0

  sc-neg : Integer -> Integer
  sc-neg (n) = let a = 5 in (-a) + 1

  sc-bool : Integer -> Integer
  sc-bool (n) = if True | False then 7 else 8

  sc-text : Integer -> Integer
  sc-text (n) = text-length "hello"

  sc-dead : Integer -> Integer
  sc-dead (n) = let u = n + 1 in 6 * 7

  sc-copy : Integer -> Integer
  sc-copy (n) = let a = n in let b = a in b + 100

  sc-once : Integer -> Integer
  sc-once (n) = let s = n * n in s + 9

  sc-cap : Integer -> Integer
  sc-cap (n) = let x = n in let n = x + 1 in n * 2

  sc-lamcap : Integer -> Integer
  sc-lamcap (n) = let x = n in (\n -> x + n) 10

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni (show (sc-fold 0))
   print-line-uni (show (sc-cmp 0))
   print-line-uni (show (sc-neg 0))
   print-line-uni (show (sc-bool 0))
   print-line-uni (show (sc-text 0))
   print-line-uni (show (sc-dead 0))
   print-line-uni (show (sc-copy 0))
   print-line-uni (show (sc-once 0))
   print-line-uni (show (sc-cap 0))
   print-line-uni (show (sc-lamcap 0))
  end
